## Changed files

- **`test/dao/stream/slice_peer.cljc`** (modified) — `:cljd` branches, all placed *first* in each reader conditional because the ClojureDart host-eval pass also matches `:clj`:
  - requires `dart:convert`, `dart:io`, and `dao.stream.ws.dart` as `host`;
  - `emit!` writes one line through `stdout.writeln`; `exit!` calls `io/exit`;
  - `:connect!` is now the Dart host's `connect!` instead of `nil`;
  - `-main` subscribes to `stdin.transform(utf8.decoder)` and reuses the existing shared `feed!` line-splitter — one isolate means stdin must be a turn on the event loop, exactly as on Node;
  - a `#?(:cljd …)` top-level `^{:dart/name main} peer-main`, because the VM starts a program at `main` and `-main` munges to `$_main`.
- **`test/dao/stream/slice_test.cljd`** (new, 612 lines) — process A on Dart: two serving endpoints over one ring buffer via `dart/bind!`/`dart/unbind!`, a `Timer.periodic` driver the test owns, and the five facts written with `await` over `Process.start`-spawned peers. Waiting is `poll-until`; nothing blocks and nothing self-schedules.
- **`bb.edn`** (modified) — `test:cljd` now compiles the peer namespace alone, AOT-compiles it to `build/slice-peer`, then runs the suite.
- **`deps.edn`** — unchanged, deliberately. The `:cljd` alias already puts `test` on the path and `cljd.build` takes explicit namespaces, so `clojure -M:cljd compile dao.stream.slice-peer` needed no new alias. Say the word if you want the peer build expressed as its own alias anyway.

Why AOT: this project's `cljd.core` carries the Flutter extensions (`package:flutter/foundation.dart` → `dart:ui`), so no ClojureDart output here runs under a plain `dart run`. An AOT executable is self-contained, which also makes it immune to the test build rewriting the same `cljd-out` tree afterwards — hence "peer first" in the task. Compiling it costs ~5s; each spawn is ~50ms. If the program is missing, `start-peer!` fails immediately naming `bb test:cljd` rather than timing out.

